<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S5.F4.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Fig. 4</span>: </span><span id="S5.F4.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
Different graph-of-thoughts structures for cooperative autonomous driving. The QA types include Perception (Q1 - Q4), Prediction (Q5 - Q7), and Planning (Q8 - Q9). If two nodes are connected by a directed edge, the answer of the parent node QA is used as the input context of the child node QA.
</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="S5.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S5.T2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">TABLE II</span>: </span><span id="S5.T2.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
Testing performance of V2V-GoT in all question-answering tasks of V2V-GoT-QA dataset, in comparison with different inference graphs.
F1: F1 score. L2: L2 distance error. L1: L1 distance error. CR: Collision rate. Comm: Communication cost. In each column, the <span id="S5.T2.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">best</span> results are in boldface.

</span></figcaption>
